cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use NEBULA in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "NEBULA: a language-independent specification for opaque rotating refresh tokens"
abstract: >-
  A precise, language-independent specification of the RFC 9700 refresh-token
  model — opaque selector/verifier tokens, rotation on every use, replay
  detection with family revocation, bounded lifetimes and optional sender
  binding — together with ten conformant reference implementations and a
  conformance suite published as machine-readable data.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Teodori
    given-names: Matteo
    # The contact of record, shared with the package manifests and the paper.
    # SUPPORT.md says what each address is for.
    email: hello@nebulatoken.dev
version: 1.0.1
# Must equal the date of the 1.0.0 tag, together with the heading in
# CHANGELOG.md. RELEASING.md carries the step that keeps the three in step.
date-released: "2026-07-30"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/nebula-token/nebula-token"
url: "https://nebulatoken.dev"
keywords:
  - refresh-token
  - token-rotation
  - replay-detection
  - authentication
  - oauth2
  - rfc9700
  - security
  - conformance-testing
#
# An archival DOI and a preferred-citation block are deliberately absent until
# the artefacts they point at exist: a DOI is minted from a published tag, and
# a preferred-citation pointing at a preprint that is not yet posted would make
# every citing tool emit a dead reference. RELEASING.md carries both as
# post-tag steps. The shape they take when they arrive:
#
# identifiers:
#   - type: doi
#     value: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX
#     description: Archived snapshot of the 1.0.0 release.
